': '#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    // ===== YOUR CODE HERE =====\n    return 0;\n}\n', 'java': 'import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // ===== YOUR CODE HERE =====\n    }\n}\n'}, 'test_cases': [{'input': '2\n2 1 5\n3 3 7\n4\n', 'expected_output': 'false', 'is_hidden': False}, {'input': '2\n2 1 5\n3 3 7\n5\n', 'expected_output': 'true', 'is_hidden': False}, {'input': '0\n0\n', 'expected_output': 'true', 'is_hidden': False}, {'input': '3\n5 0 10\n5 5 15\n5 10 20\n9\n', 'expected_output': 'false', 'is_hidden': True}, {'input': '3\n5 0 10\n5 5 15\n5 10 20\n10\n', 'expected_output': 'true', 'is_hidden': True}]}, {'title': 'Check if Array Is Sorted and Rotated', 'slug': 'check-if-array-is-sorted-and-rotated', 'difficulty': 'EASY', 'topic': 'ARRAY', 'description': '# Is Rotated Sorted Array?\n\n## Statement\nGiven an integer array `nums`, determine whether it could have been produced by taking a non‑decreasing sequence, possibly containing duplicates, and rotating it by some number of positions (including zero). Return `true` if such a rotation exists, otherwise `false`.\n\n## Input Format\n- Line 1: integer `n` – the length of the array.\n- Line 2: `n` integers separated by spaces – the elements of `nums`.\n\n## Output Format\nPrint a single word: `true` or `false`.\n\n## Constraints\n- `1 ≤ n ≤ 10^4`\n- `1 ≤ nums[i] ≤ 10^9`\n\n## Example\n**Input**\n```\n5\n3 4 5 1 2\n```\n**Output**\n```\ntrue\n```\n', 'starter_code': {'python': 'import sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    nums = list(map(int, data[1:1+n]))\n    # ===== YOUR CODE HERE =====\n    # Your code should compute the answer and print it\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n', 'cpp': '#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespac